 "switcher_quotes": [
  {
   "app": "memrise",
   "score": 5,
   "content": "Excellent app and way of learning a language. I used Duolingo for many years and I prefer Memrise. It uses a lot of the same methods, but the videos and the AI chat are a great way to augment the learning, and the slightly less gamified approach is much less stressful than Duolin"
  },
  {
   "app": "babbel",
   "score": 5,
   "content": "I've tried Duolingo (useless), Memrise, and Rosetta Stone (the best, but expensive and intense), but Babbel is my favorite. Babble is effective, engaging, and fun. Currently studying Italian. The lessons nicely combine memorization with grammar, so you learn words and also learn "
  },
  {
   "app": "memrise",
   "score": 5,
